WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:02.890
Almost every superhero has an evil opposite.

00:00:02.890 --> 00:00:08.170
Spider-Man has Venom, Superman has Bizarro,
and Shazam the hero formerly known as Captain

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:11.710
Marvel has the deadliest of them all: Black
Adam.

00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:15.580
Powered by the same mystical lightning that
makes his nemesis so formidable, Adam has

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:19.449
all of Shazam's powers, and is far more ruthless
in using them.

00:00:19.449 --> 00:00:23.670
He's easily one of DC's most popular villains,
but that wasn't always the case.

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:26.660
Here’s the untold truth of Black Adam!

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:28.420
Black Adam appears

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:32.330
To say that Captain Marvel was popular in
the '40s might be the biggest understatement

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:34.090
in superhero history.

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:39.250
Captain Marvel Adventures legendarily outsold
Superman, and in 1945, Fawcett launched yet

00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:44.329
another comic for Cap and his sidekicks that
would run for 89 issues: The Marvel Family.

00:00:44.329 --> 00:00:46.870
For the launch of a new magazine, Otto Binder
and C.C.

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:51.010
Beck knew they needed a pretty big story,
so they put a new spin on an idea they’d

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:55.559
already tried with a villain named IBAC who
was powered by history’s greatest evils.

00:00:55.559 --> 00:00:59.460
In "The Mighty Marvels Join Forces," they
revealed that Billy Batson wasn't the first

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:01.609
mortal to wield the power of Shazam.

00:01:01.609 --> 00:01:06.220
The original was Teth-Adam, an Egyptian man
who lived 5,000 years ago, and who was chosen

00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:09.040
for what the wizard saw as the purity of his
soul.

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:13.000
Unfortunately, power corrupts, and being the
most powerful person on Earth quickly went

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:14.270
to Adam's head.

00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:18.970
After snapping a Pharaoh's neck a bit of violence
that's pretty shocking by Shazam standards

00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:23.180
Adam was exiled by the wizard to "the farthest
star," from which it coincidentally took him

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:25.140
about 5,000 years to return.

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:29.280
When the Marvel Family tricked him into saying
"Shazam," all that time caught up with him,

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:33.490
and Teth-Adam quickly aged so fast that he
turned to dust before their eyes.

00:01:33.490 --> 00:01:37.520
And believe it or not, that's how he stayed
for the next 30 years.

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:39.150
Back in Black

00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:44.240
After crumbling to dust in 1945, Black Adam
wasn't seen again until DC started publishing

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:48.790
Shazam in the '70s with the title changed
because Marvel Comics had snapped up "Captain

00:01:48.790 --> 00:01:52.040
Marvel" in 1967 for their own cosmic hero.

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:56.910
In Shazam #28, Dr. Sivana (with an assist
from Otto Binder and legendary Superman artist

00:01:56.910 --> 00:02:01.450
Kurt Schaffenberger) employed a "Reincarnation
Machine" to bring Adam back to life and set

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:03.450
him loose to destroy Boston.

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:07.090
Unfortunately for Adam, his second outing
wound up going exactly the same way as his

00:02:07.090 --> 00:02:10.420
first one, right down to being tricked into
saying "Shazam."

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:14.390
This time, though, he stuck around long enough
to cement himself as one of the Shazam family's

00:02:14.390 --> 00:02:16.240
greatest foes.

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:17.860
What's in a (magic) name?

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:21.940
If you're up on your comics trivia, you're
probably aware that Shazam's magic word gave

00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:27.650
him the attributes of six mythological patrons:
the wisdom of Solomon, the strength of Hercules,

00:02:27.650 --> 00:02:32.890
the courage of Achilles, the power of Zeus,
the stamina of Atlas, and the speed of Mercury.

00:02:32.890 --> 00:02:36.750
Considering how similar they are, you might
assume that Black Adam drew from the same

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:40.700
sources for his own powers, but that turned
out to not be the case.

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:44.920
When Billy realized that being 5,000 years
old put Black Adam squarely before the time

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:49.270
of wise King Solomon, the wizard explained
that he was powered by Egyptian deities, with

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:54.590
the stamina of Shu, the strength of Hershef,
the power of Amon, the wisdom of Zehuti, the

00:02:54.590 --> 00:02:56.910
speed of Anpu, and the courage of Menthu.

00:02:56.910 --> 00:03:00.790
If a few of those don't sound too familiar,
well, that’s because Binder fudged it a

00:03:00.790 --> 00:03:03.480
little, using lesser-known names for a few
of the gods.

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:08.720
Zehuti and Anpu, for instance, are definitely
more well known as Thoth and Anubis.

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:12.650
As for why he bothered to change Anubis, when
it already fit the acronym, your guess is

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:14.210
as good as ours.

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:16.120
Theo Adam and the Power of Shazam

00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:21.720
In 1987, the Shazam Family was formally inducted
into the DC Universe following Crisis on Infinite

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:26.140
Earths, but with all his similarities to Superman,
it didn't really work until writer/artist

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:29.880
Jerry Ordway relaunched The Power of Shazam
in 1994.

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:33.490
One of Ordway's biggest changes in updating
Captain Marvel for the '90s came from the

00:03:33.490 --> 00:03:35.610
way he reimagined Black Adam.

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:39.310
He was the first creator to make Adam into
the book's primary villain from the start

00:03:39.310 --> 00:03:42.430
not just for Captain Marvel, but for Billy
Batson, too.

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:46.090
Rather than just being an ancient Egyptian
warrior, Ordway's take gave the villain a

00:03:46.090 --> 00:03:51.240
modern-day secret identity: Theo Adam, a greedy
archaeologist who accompanied Billy’s parents

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:55.650
on a dig, and eliminated them in a fit of
rage in order to get his hands on a priceless

00:03:55.650 --> 00:03:56.650
artifact.

00:03:56.650 --> 00:03:57.650
Even worse?

00:03:57.650 --> 00:04:01.750
That artifact allowed him to transform into
Black Adam, becoming Captain Marvel's first

00:04:01.750 --> 00:04:03.630
and greatest arch-nemesis.

00:04:03.630 --> 00:04:07.640
Not only was he his evil opposite, he was
also the guy who took his parents from him,

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:10.380
mixing a touch of Batman into Billy's origin.

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:15.670
In 1999, Ordway would add another interesting
twist when Adam started saving people, and

00:04:15.670 --> 00:04:20.180
even turned himself into the Justice League,
claiming to be innocent of Theo Adam’s crimes.

00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:24.810
In both an earthly courtroom and a mystical
trial, he proved that Theo Adam and Teth-Adam

00:04:24.810 --> 00:04:29.210
were actually two different people who happened
to share a body due to the wizard's magic,

00:04:29.210 --> 00:04:33.080
and that every evil act had been done under
Theo's influence before Teth-Adam had been

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:34.780
able to regain control.

00:04:34.780 --> 00:04:38.400
With that, Adam was reformed… more or less.

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:42.280
While he still occasionally found himself
operating as a supervillain due to Theo’s

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:46.650
lingering influence, Adam was heroic enough
that he even joined the Justice Society of

00:04:46.650 --> 00:04:47.900
America.

00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:50.560
The ultra-violent king of Kahndaq

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:55.130
Remember how Black Adam's very first appearance
in 1945 started off with him snapping a dude's

00:04:55.130 --> 00:04:56.960
neck and taking over his country?

00:04:56.960 --> 00:05:01.520
Despite his seeming reformation, that tendency
towards shocking on-panel violence was something

00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:05.060
that remained a part of Adam's character all
the way through the modern age and in the

00:05:05.060 --> 00:05:08.030
21st century, it was ramped up to the extreme.

00:05:08.030 --> 00:05:12.530
His most famous act of ridiculously over-the-top
brutality came when he shoved the Psycho Pirate's

00:05:12.530 --> 00:05:16.280
eyes through the back of his head, but he
also vanquished Terra from the Teen Titans

00:05:16.280 --> 00:05:20.650
by punching through her torso, and at one
point, after being stripped of his powers,

00:05:20.650 --> 00:05:22.530
even resorted to cannibalism.

00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:27.280
The idea, it seems, was to make him as dark
as Shazam was bright, but it's easy to argue

00:05:27.280 --> 00:05:29.590
that creators of that era went too far.

00:05:29.590 --> 00:05:34.340
When Black Adam was rebooted once again in
2011, he was still undeniably villainous,

00:05:34.340 --> 00:05:37.710
but that level of blood and gore was apparently
left behind.

00:05:37.710 --> 00:05:40.040
If you smell what Black Adam's cookin'

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:44.860
The biggest piece of Black Adam news to come
along… well, ever, has undoubtedly been

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:48.160
the casting of Dwayne "The Rock" Johnson in
DC's cinematic universe.

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:53.120
In 2014, after years of speculation, it was
revealed that Johnson will be taking on the

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:57.570
role of Teth-Adam, perhaps making his first
appearance in the sequel to Suicide Squad.

00:05:57.570 --> 00:06:01.620
As exciting as that is, it's also pretty surprising
for Johnson to be cast as the villain.

00:06:01.620 --> 00:06:06.070
Shazam is based on the childhood power fantasy
of a kid who can transform into the coolest

00:06:06.070 --> 00:06:07.570
adult he can imagine.

00:06:07.570 --> 00:06:11.199
With that in mind, he seems like a much more
natural fit for the hero what kid wouldn't

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:13.320
want to say a magic word and turn into the
Rock?

